#!/bin/sh
# Start THE desktop. There is exactly one: /OS/bin/desktop (the AES application that
# used to be called `aesdesk`; the old gem_wm demo of the same name is retired).
#
# This script lived ONLY on the SD card for a while, which meant the repo could not keep
# it correct: when the binary was renamed, the card kept launching a stale `aesdesk` and
# the board looked fine while running months-old code. It is in-tree now so `make
# sdstage` owns it. Do not "fix" it by editing the card.
/OS/bin/desktop &
